h2:generating-model-based-predicted-probabilities Generating model-based predicted probabilities
fig:logitmdp Predicted probability of supporting the death penalty across levels of education for White, non-Hispanic male respondents, with 95 percent confidence intervals.
fig:logitpredictions Predicted probabilities of supporting the death penalty by sex and educational attainment (White, non-Hispanic), from less than high school (1) to graduate degree (5). The error bars (95 percent confidence intervals) overlap, displaying the lack of statistically significant difference between sexes at each level of educational attainment.
h3:quick-package-functions-for-model-based-predictions Quick package functions for model-based predictions
fig:predictoreffects Panel of predicted probabilities from the \\textbf{effects} package. The \\texttt{predictorEffects()} function creates a graphic displaying predicted probabilities across each range of each independent variable.  For each panel, all other independent variables are held at a mean (for numeric) or reference category (for factor) variables.
